From 128d3d5e1b55ef661621c1009f76ba453ab3075a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:00:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: a passthrough packet left out moves the readings of
 the average

A passthrough stream that is behind the video is put back by leaving
packets out (SyncStream(), SYNC_ADJUST). Each one moves the error by
exactly one frame, which is credited to the error in hand
(CSyncError::Correction()), but the readings summed for the next average
were taken before it and keep the error from before it. Where packets are
left out faster than the average is renewed, the next average brings that
error back and the correction goes on past the video. A run of packets
left out at once is what a late start of TrueHD gives once its cache is
no longer turned into pauses by the measure (next commit): measured on
the host, a TrueHD start 600 ms late on a device of 100 ms then ended
119 ms ahead of the video, against 30 ms or less with this.

The readings summed so far are now moved by the same frame
(CSyncError::MoveReadings()). Only for a packet left out: a pause moves
the error by what the packer makes of it (whole periods of its bursts),
which the readings after it measure. Moved by the pause asked for as
well, DTS-HD MA stopped at the edge of the band, 30.2 to 40.8 ms from
the video where it had landed within 20 ms, in 24 cases of the host
harness of the sync. PCM, transcoding and what the player is told are
as before.
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp     | 5 +++++
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAEStream.h | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
index 5f4c6f8..cbad83f 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAE.cpp
@@ -3439,6 +3439,11 @@ CSampleBuffer* CActiveAE::SyncStream(CActiveAEStream *stream)
         if (-error > stream->m_format.m_streamInfo.GetDuration() * scale / 2)
         {
           stream->m_syncError.Correction(stream->m_format.m_streamInfo.GetDuration() * scale);
+          // Hades: the readings summed so far for the next average were taken before the packet was
+          // left out, which moves the error by exactly its frame: they are moved too, or a run of
+          // packets left out at once brings the error from before them back and goes past it. (A
+          // pause moves it by what the packer makes of it, which the readings after it measure.)
+          stream->m_syncError.MoveReadings(stream->m_format.m_streamInfo.GetDuration() * scale);
           error += stream->m_format.m_streamInfo.GetDuration() * scale;
           buf->pkt->nb_samples = 0;
           stream->m_rawDropped++; // (Hades)
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAEStream.h b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAEStream.h
index 1c45f65..6e2ae72 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAEStream.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAEStream.h
@@ -92,6 +92,11 @@ public:
     m_lastError += correction;
   }
 
+  //! Hades: a passthrough packet left out for the sync moves the error by exactly its frame: the
+  //! readings summed so far for the next average, each taken before it, are moved as much
+  //! (CActiveAE::SyncStream())
+  void MoveReadings(double correction) { m_buffer += correction * m_count; }
+
   //! Hades: the time that the average under way still has (a pause of passthrough keeps it)
   std::chrono::milliseconds GetTimeLeft() const { return m_timer.GetTimeLeft(); }
 
